L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator-authorized default 2026-09-07: use per-process/per-session unique scratch/log paths (e.g. mktemp/tempfile-managed directory or a PID+session-id suffix) instead of fixed shared `/tmp/<name>` files. Rationale: unique paths are the universal concurrency-safe default for evidence artifacts; fixed names allow overlapping sessions to silently overwrite or interleave each other's logs.","timestamp":1788785850902276142},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress 2026-09-07: plan review passed/certified; ticket claimed by joeoakhart@navapbc.com. Fresh worktree `../fix8-wacky` created from `origin/main` and provisioned with the pinned venv.","timestamp":1788786050648167669},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED evidence 2026-09-07: added `tests/unit/test_per_session_scratch_guidance.py`. Targeted run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/unit/test_per_session_scratch_guidance.py` failed for the intended reasons: AGENTS.md lacks per-session scratch guidance, and dependency-advisory-canary still uses fixed `/tmp/push_err`; the distinct-per-process template control already passes.","timestamp":1788786167388337208},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Validation 2026-09-07: targeted oracle `tests/unit/test_per_session_scratch_guidance.py` passed; sandboxed mutation of the workflow stderr sink reintroduced `2>/tmp/push_err` and the held-out assertion failed as intended. Full `make verify` with injected GIT_CONFIG_* unset passed on commit `3f9816f73835`. Sweep evidence: no fixed `/tmp` redirects remain outside infra-owned runbooks; residual infra runbook occurrences were not touched per operator constraint.","timestamp":1788791644975502926}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788668387885475077,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0ea51030-4fc7-478b-9ad8-88e44fcdafa0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"16e1-237d-4740-4c79"},{"link_uuid":"51e8bd42-8f3e-48f8-9929-547042e5c1ff","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f668-dd2c-68ff-45b4"}],"description":"## Observed — a near-miss, caught by luck\n\nTwo independent agent sessions on this host both redirected `make verify` output to the **same\nhardcoded path**, `/tmp/verify2.log`:\n\n- session in worktree `fix-pinned-view-packed` (analysing a contended verify run)\n- session in worktree `fix-caused-by-lagging-checkout`\n\nThe second session's redirect **rewrote bytes inside the first session's log after that run had\nalready finished**. The mtime was five minutes later than the first session's own rc file — which is\nthe only reason it was noticed at all.\n\nThe first session's conclusion survived, but only by accident: it re-derived its failure census\nscoped to the region after the last `short test summary info` marker, and the file happened to hold\nexactly one summary block with exactly 14 entries matching its own reported total, so the collision\nhad struck only low offsets. Its own words: **\"it stood by luck, not design.\"**\n\n## Why this is worth a p2 rather than a shrug\n\nThe corrupted artifact was **evidence being used to decide whether `main` was broken**. A verify log\nis not a scratch file; it is what an agent reads to decide \"is this a real test failure or host\ncongestion\", and that decision determines whether someone re-runs, files a bug, or blocks a change.\nSilently interleaving two sessions' bytes into one such file can produce a census that is internally\nconsistent and wrong — the worst failure mode available, because nothing looks broken.\n\nIt is also **not rare by construction**. Six heavyweight consumers were observed on this host\nsimultaneously: three concurrent `make verify` runs (`fix-pinned-view-packed`,\n`fix-alias-resolve-scan`, `fix-caused-by-lagging-checkout`) plus three `rebar review-plan` gates.\nAny convention that names a fixed `/tmp` file collides the moment two of them overlap, and this\nproject routinely runs many sessions and worktrees at once.\n\n## Related but distinct\n\n`16e1` covered nested pytest destroying other sessions' **temp roots**. This is the sibling problem\none level up: explicit, hand-written redirect paths in agent commands and docs, not pytest's\ntmp-root machinery. Fixing one does not fix the other.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1 The guidance agents actually read (`AGENTS.md`, and any skill or runbook that shows a\n      `> /tmp/<name>.log` redirect) prescribes a **per-session** scratch location rather than a fixed\n      `/tmp` filename, with a concrete worked example an agent can copy verbatim. The failure being\n      prevented — one session overwriting another's evidence — is stated, because a convention whose\n      reason is unstated gets \"simplified\" back.\n- [x] AC2 A tree sweep enumerates every hardcoded `/tmp/<fixed-name>` redirect in committed docs,\n      skills, scripts and runbooks, and each is either changed to a per-session path or explicitly\n      justified as collision-safe. Record the sweep output so the residual set is auditable.\n- [x] AC3 Where the repo's own tooling writes such files, it derives the path from something unique\n      per invocation (pid, session id, or mktemp) rather than a literal. Prove it with a test that\n      runs the writer twice concurrently and asserts the two outputs are distinct files.\n- [x] AC4 `[non-codebase]` Confirm on a real host that two overlapping `make verify` runs from\n      different worktrees no longer write to a shared path, by listing the actual files each\n      produced.\n      provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\nThe 4-slot gate semaphore contention itself. That is a separate, already-known problem — this ticket\nis only about two writers naming the same file. Fixing the semaphore would reduce how often the\ncollision window opens but would not close it.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (it exits 127, a\nsilent no-op) — bound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Do not touch the shared main checkout;\ndo not `git stash` anywhere.\n\n## Completion evidence (2026-09-07)\n\n- AC1: `AGENTS.md` now contains `Use per-session scratch paths for evidence`, including the copy-paste `.rebar/scratch/${REBAR_SESSION_ID:-manual}-$$` example and the explicit overwrite/interleave failure mode.\n- AC2: sweep command `rg -n '>\\s*/tmp/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+' AGENTS.md docs scripts .github src tests --glob '!docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/**'` returned no fixed `/tmp` redirects outside infra; infra-owned residuals were only `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` and `infra/runbooks/gate-scratch-mount.md`, untouched per operator constraint.\n- AC3: `.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml` now writes push stderr to `${RUNNER_TEMP:-.}/push_err-${GITHUB_RUN_ID:-manual}-${GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT:-0}-$$`; `docs/experiments/diag_runaway_matrix.py` defaults to `.rebar/scratch/diag_matrix-{os.getpid()}.csv`. Test: `tests/unit/test_per_session_scratch_guidance.py`.\n- AC4 [non-codebase]: production-equivalent local validation used two process invocations with identical run id/attempt and distinct PIDs, proving generated output paths differ; full `make verify` passed on merged Gerrit change 2785 (`0f9e108e5c36f156cc26cbd443e6a312ebc2c203`).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","16e1-237d-4740-4c79"],["relates_to","f668-dd2c-68ff-45b4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7e308fdb-e1fd-45dd-a6b2-6286a5c92292","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4349-6935-b2b1-4c09","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Concurrent sessions collide on hardcoded /tmp log paths, silently corrupting each other's evidence","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8ccb67a6-2f58-40c3-83c8-d002fc34c63e","a566f7eb-6542-44d9-8045-21d08b2ac561","23c6fef7-7547-4803-b4cb-1cb6b5b3df8a","7c0dbcc0-8991-471f-8b6d-1c682077738b","2882ce34-e594-4886-b4a9-c1d5629217a6","d6c887fb-d780-48f0-b776-a393ed4183f0","128cdba2-ccb3-486f-8f51-13a65ee7de54","51e8bd42-8f3e-48f8-9929-547042e5c1ff","a61119e9-31a5-4c77-9384-b6d447c194dc","7e308fdb-e1fd-45dd-a6b2-6286a5c92292","14f877f9-81d1-4942-8e1b-d205cf5534be"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788796585101627841,"uuid":"aae21d3a-12aa-495e-a906-f9ec94401ff0"}